@startuml Simulation Engine Sequence Diagram

!define ASYNC_COLOR #LightBlue
!define SYNC_COLOR #LightCoral
!define DATA_COLOR #LightGreen
!define EVENT_COLOR #Orange

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Simulation Engine - Event-Driven Architecture Sequence

actor "User" as user
participant "sim-engine-frontend" as frontend #LightYellow
participant "sim-engine-backend" as backend #23c6b7
queue "Message Broker" as broker #LightYellow
participant "calculation-engine" as calcEngine #LightGreen
database "Source Database" as sourceDB #LightGray
database "Object Storage\n(Result Chunks)" as objStorage #LightBlue
participant "simulation-engine" as simEngine #23c6b7
database "Simulation DB" as simDB #LightGray

== Simulation Submission ==

user -> frontend: Initiate simulation
frontend -> backend: HTTPS REST\nPOST /simulation
activate backend
backend -> broker: Publish event:\n**simulation.requested**
backend --> frontend: HTTP 202 Accepted\n(simulation_id)
deactivate backend
frontend -> backend: HTTPS GET\nPoll status
note right of frontend: Periodic polling\nor SSE connection

== Calculation Phase ==

broker -> calcEngine: Consume:\n**simulation.requested**
activate calcEngine

calcEngine -> sourceDB: Native DB protocol\nSQL query
activate sourceDB
sourceDB --> calcEngine: Stream result set
deactivate sourceDB

calcEngine -> objStorage: Write Parquet chunks
note right of calcEngine: Split large results\ninto manageable chunks

calcEngine -> broker: Publish event:\n**calculation.completed**
deactivate calcEngine

== Persistence Phase ==

broker -> simEngine: Consume:\n**calculation.completed**
activate simEngine

simEngine -> objStorage: Read result chunks
activate objStorage
objStorage --> simEngine: Parquet data
deactivate objStorage

simEngine -> simDB: Bulk load data
activate simDB
simDB --> simEngine: Load success
deactivate simDB

simEngine -> broker: Publish event:\n**persistence.completed**
deactivate simEngine

== Status Update ==

broker -> backend: Consume:\n**persistence.completed**
activate backend
backend --> frontend: Status update\n(via polling or SSE)
deactivate backend

frontend --> user: Display results

note over frontend, simDB
  **Key Design Patterns:**
  - Async event-driven architecture
  - Chunked data processing for large datasets
  - Decoupled computation and persistence
  - Polling or SSE for status updates
end note

@enduml

